      <section class="section-faq">
        <div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container-1280 w-container">
          <div id="contact" class="faq-wrapper">
            <div class="left_side-faq">
              <div class="header-faq">
                <div class="text_heading-faq">
                  <div class="text-12-caps opacity-60 center-small">Frequently asked questions</div>
                  <div class="max-w-400">
                    <h2 class="h2 center-small"><span class="span-pink-2">Got questions?</span> <br>We&#x27;ve got answers</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80 center-small">We want to make sure you feel confident that our service is right for you. Here we’ve looked to address some commonly asked questions. If you have any more specific questions, don’t hesitate to get in touch with a member of the team.</p>
              </div><img src="/images/Frame-1707478606_4.avif" loading="lazy" alt="An abstract digital interface featuring a dark theme with various input fields, a progress bar, and a question mark icon, suggesting a user-friendly design for a software application." class="image-faq">
            </div>
            <div class="right_side-faq">
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="1b125ce8-0131-b0c5-5248-9c8466cfd7a3" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <p class="text-14-150">What are UI design services?</p>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="1b125ce8-0131-b0c5-5248-9c8466cfd7a7" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav style="height:0px" class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">UI (User Interface) design services encompass the creation and optimization of visual elements and interactive components that users engage with in digital products. Our UI design services include:</p>
                    <ul role="list" class="list-item-faq numbers">
                      <li>Web UI Design: Creating stunning, responsive web interfaces that enhance user experience across all devices.</li>
                      <li>Mobile App UI Design: Designing intuitive and engaging mobile app interfaces for iOS and Android platforms.</li>
                      <li>Dashboard UI Design: Developing clear, data-driven dashboards that simplify complex information for easy decision-making.</li>
                      <li>UI Style Guide Creation: Establishing consistent design languages and component libraries for scalable product development.</li>
                      <li>Prototype Development: Building interactive prototypes to test and refine user flows before full development.</li>
                      <li>UI Redesign &amp; Optimization: Enhancing existing interfaces to improve usability, accessibility, and conversion rates.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">Our UI designers go beyond creating visually appealing interfaces; we understand the core components that define success or failure in user interface design.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="16bdd7f2-f178-dc89-1aa3-d17e63ce0acc" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <p class="text-14-150">How much does UI design service cost?</p>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="16bdd7f2-f178-dc89-1aa3-d17e63ce0ad0" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav style="height:0px" class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">The cost of UI design services can vary significantly depending on the scope and complexity of your project. Factors that influence the cost include:</p>
                    <ul role="list" class="list-item-faq numbers">
                      <li>The type of project (web, mobile app, dashboard, etc.)</li>
                      <li>The number of screens or pages to be designed</li>
                      <li>The level of interactivity and complexity required</li>
                      <li>The need for additional services like research, prototyping, or style guide creation</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">We offer flexible pricing options to accommodate different project needs and budgets. For a more accurate estimate, we recommend contacting us directly to discuss your specific project requirements. We can then provide a tailored quote based on your needs.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="cd51e8db-4393-5835-0273-3b02d3c11142" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <p class="text-14-150">What is the difference between UX and UI design?</p>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="cd51e8db-4393-5835-0273-3b02d3c11146" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav style="height:0px" class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">While UX (User Experience) and UI (User Interface) design are closely related and often overlap, they focus on different aspects of the product design process:<br><br>UX Design:</p>
                    <ul role="list" class="list-item-faq">
                      <li>Focuses on the overall feel of the experience</li>
                      <li>Involves understanding user needs, behaviors, and motivations</li>
                      <li>Includes research, user flows, wireframing, and prototyping</li>
                      <li>Aims to solve user problems and create a smooth, efficient experience</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">UI Design:</p>
                    <ul role="list" class="list-item-faq">
                      <li>Focuses on the visual and interactive elements of a product</li>
                      <li>Involves creating the look and feel of the interface</li>
                      <li>Includes designing layouts, choosing color schemes, typography, and creating interactive elements</li>
                      <li>Aims to create visually appealing and intuitive interfaces that align with the brand</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">At Motion The Agency, our UI designers work closely with UX principles to ensure that our designs are not only visually appealing but also user-friendly and effective.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
              <div data-delay="0" data-hover="false" data-w-id="f244105a-4a61-59de-8011-4f0ff09f2ed2" class="dropdown-faq w-dropdown">
                <div class="dropdown-top w-dropdown-toggle">
                  <p class="text-14-150">Do UI designers make wireframes?</p>
                  <div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="ic-plus-faq" data-w-id="f244105a-4a61-59de-8011-4f0ff09f2ed6" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/62581cacf7654a9838775673/62581cacf7654a49f0775692_plus.json" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="0.5" data-duration="0" data-loading="eager"></div>
                </div>
                <nav style="height:0px" class="dropdown-list-faq w-dropdown-list">
                  <div class="wrapper-text-faq">
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">Yes, UI designers often create wireframes as part of the design process. Wireframing is typically one of the early stages in our UI design process, following the Discovery and Research &amp; Analysis phases.<br><br>As mentioned in our process section:</p>
                    <ul role="list" class="list-item-faq numbers">
                      <li>We start by understanding your business goals, target audience, and project requirements.</li>
                      <li>We conduct user research, competitive analysis, and define user personas to inform our design strategy.</li>
                      <li>We create low-fidelity wireframes to establish the layout and structure of the interface.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">Wireframes serve as a blueprint for the interface, allowing us to focus on the structure and functionality before moving on to the visual design phase. They help in:</p>
                    <ul role="list" class="list-item-faq">
                      <li>Establishing the basic structure of a page or screen</li>
                      <li>Defining the layout and hierarchy of content</li>
                      <li>Planning user flows and interactions</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-14-150 opacity-80">After the wireframing stage, we move on to creating high-fidelity designs and interactive prototypes, refining the design based on feedback and testing.</p>
                  </div>
                </nav>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
